## 1011. Capacity to check packages within D days.
## Leetcode link: https://leetcode.com/problems/capacity-to-ship-packages-within-d-days/

The problem asks for the minimum ship capacity to finish within given days.
Whenever we see “minimum possible value”, that hints toward searching over answers.

The capacity has a monotonic behavior:

If a certain capacity works,

Any larger capacity will also work.
This monotonic property allows Binary Search.

The capacity range is obvious:

Minimum = max(weights) (must carry heaviest package)

Maximum = sum(weights) (ship all in one day)

So instead of guessing randomly, we binary search this range and check feasibility.

## Approach

Set low = max(weights) and high = sum(weights).

While low <= high, pick mid as possible capacity.

Simulate shipping greedily and count how many days are needed.

If required days ≤ given days → try smaller capacity (high = mid - 1).

Otherwise → increase capacity (low = mid + 1).

Return low as the minimum valid capacity.

## Complexity

Time: O(n log(sum))

Space: O(1)



/**
 * @param {number[]} weights
 * @param {number} days
 * @return {number}
 */
var shipWithinDays = function(weights, days) {
    let n=weights.length;
    let low=Math.max(...weights);
    let high= weights.reduce((accumulator, currentValue) => {
        return accumulator + currentValue;
    }, 0);
      
    while(low<=high){
        let sum=0;
        let c=1;
        let mid = Math.floor((low + high) / 2);
        for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
            if(sum+weights[i]>mid){
                sum=weights[i];
                c++;
            }else{
                sum+=weights[i];
            }
        }
        if(c<=days)high=mid-1;
        else low=mid+1;
    }
    return low;
};
